-- title:
--   Mod p Galois representation from a weight-two Hecke character
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $N \ge 1$ a natural number and $S$ an arbitrary set of natural numbers. Let $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) be the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` attached to the primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to the primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$. Let $\kappa$ be a field of characteristic $p$, assume given a ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$ to $\kappa$, and let $\chi \colon \mathbb{T} \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism. Then there is a group homomorphism $\rho \colon \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(\kappa)$, where $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, with the following four properties. First, $\rho$ factors through a finite level: there is an intermediate field $L$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$, such that $\rho\sigma = 1$ for every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise. Second, for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ and $\ell \neq p$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, one has $\mathrm{tr}\,\rho(\sigma) = \chi(T_\ell)$, where $T_\ell$ is [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L77) for the data $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$. Third, under the same hypotheses but without the condition $\ell \notin S$, $\det \rho(\sigma) = \ell$ in $\kappa$. Fourth, for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \neq p$ and every such $A$, $\rho$ is trivial on the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   This is the residual representation attached to a mod $p$ system of Hecke eigenvalues in weight two and level $\Gamma_0(N)$, in the form produced by Eichler–Shimura theory on $J_0(N)$, here transported from its field of definition to an arbitrary characteristic $p$ coefficient field $\kappa$ receiving the algebraic integers. It is obtained from the corresponding statement over a finite field for a maximal ideal of the Hecke algebra containing $p$, together with the finiteness of the Hecke algebra as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module, and feeds the construction of Galois representations attached to eigensystems in the first cohomology.
